# `txb_coeff_satd`'s two internal buffers hoisted into a per-thread scratch.
#
# host  : mac (Apple M4 Pro, aarch64-apple-darwin)
# tool  : tools/perf_ab.sh — interleaved paired rounds, order randomised per
#         round, one untimed warmup inside each sample, NEITHER SIDE NICED,
#         no -C target-cpu=native
# base  : the `dqcoeff` hoist commit          cand: + this hoist
# grid  : gradient qp 40; still 256/512 x p{2,6,10} n=15,
#         videokey (SVTAV1_VIDEO=1) 128/256/512 x p{6,8} n=25
# ident : Y on all twelve cells
#
# WHY THIS SITE. Second largest allocation SITE in the encoder after
# `tx_pipeline::tx_unit_inner` — 28,006 calls to the allocator on ONE 512x512
# video-mode key frame at preset 8 (heaptrack --print-allocators, r7900x),
# two `vec![0i32; w*h]` per call, neither escaping.
#
# RESULT — and it is the largest single win of the day, at the SLOW presets:
#   still     256 p2  1.034x  (p25/p75 0.9633/0.9681)
#             512 p2  1.029x  (0.9694/0.9740)
#             256 p6  1.008x | 512 p6 1.012x
#             256 p10 1.003x | 512 p10 0.991x  <- the one cell that goes the
#                                                 wrong way; its span crosses
#                                                 1.0 and it is NULL, not a
#                                                 regression
#   videokey  256 p6  1.013x | 512 p6 1.016x   (both spans below 1.0)
#             128 p6  1.002x | 128 p8 0.999x | 256 p8 1.003x | 512 p8 1.009x
#
# THE SHAPE OF THE RESULT IS THE INTERESTING PART: it concentrates at the SLOW
# presets, which is where the candidate set is widest and the chroma detector
# runs most. A p10-only measurement would have called this NULL. That is the
# same lesson the tile-reservation record carries from the size axis: sweep the
# axis the mechanism is keyed on, or you will report one cell's answer as the
# answer.
#
# NOT ESTABLISHED: that the remaining ~170k per-frame allocations
# (`extract_neighbors_tiled` 31,696, `mds3::eval_candidate` 25,799,
# `pd0::lvl1_cost_from_pred` 25,160, `cost_coeffs_txb` 19,553,
# `pd0::tx_quant_core` 15,096, `inject_candidates` 12,064,
# `md_cfl_rd_pick_alpha` 9,280) would scale this. Each needs its own
# measurement; two of them return their buffers to the caller and cannot take
# this shape at all.
